{
  "chapter": "STARTING_OUT_WITH_LINES",
  "description": "Your journey into industrial plastics begins with §aPolyethylene§r. Produce it by reacting §eOxygen§r with §eEthylene§r on §6Program 1§r in a chemical reactor. Your initial batches will be made in §bSingleblock Chemical Reactors§r, then you'll upgrade to the more efficient §bLarge Chemical Reactor§r at §bHV§r tier.

(Be aware of the alternate recipe using §eAir§r; it offers lower yield and is  more challenging to obtain in sufficient quantity.)

Initially, the primary use of §aPolyethylene§r is crafting §dHV Machine Hulls§r from its sheets. It can also be processed in an §bAssembler§r to conserve more valuable §dmaterials plates§r. Looking ahead, §aPolyethylene§r is critical for making §dPlastic Circuit Boards§r for the  §bMicro-Processor§r circuit line.",
